WEBVTT

00:11.720 --> 00:13.805
♪ See the daylight ♪

00:14.681 --> 00:17.392
♪ Covering the sky ♪

00:18.351 --> 00:21.730
♪ Hear the wind say ♪

00:21.813 --> 00:25.567
♪ No matter what you do, my friend ♪

00:25.650 --> 00:29.195
♪ You know the world
Still needs your light ♪

00:29.279 --> 00:31.865
♪ Let it just shine ♪

00:31.948 --> 00:33.992
♪ You'll be free ♪

00:34.075 --> 00:37.912
♪ From all the things you used to be ♪

00:40.040 --> 00:42.500
- [train passing]
- [bell clanging]

00:45.045 --> 00:49.382
DOONA!

00:50.675 --> 00:52.802
[birds chirping]

00:52.886 --> 00:53.970
[Won-jun humming]

00:54.054 --> 00:55.722
[gentle music playing]

01:06.483 --> 01:07.525
[Doona growls]

01:07.609 --> 01:09.486
- [Won-jun] Ah, you're so heavy!
- [both laugh]

01:10.779 --> 01:12.405
[Doona laughing]

01:12.489 --> 01:14.783
[both laughing]

01:16.743 --> 01:18.620
- Muah!
- [both laugh]

01:39.057 --> 01:40.850
- Hell there.
- Hello.

01:40.934 --> 01:42.477
[Doona] They're all so pretty.

01:42.560 --> 01:44.604
Please let me know
if you have any questions.

01:49.234 --> 01:50.110
That's pretty.

01:50.193 --> 01:51.111
- [Doona] Is it?
- Mm-hmm.

01:51.194 --> 01:53.113
- [woman] We have a matching one for men.
- You do?

01:53.613 --> 01:54.823
Here you go.

01:54.906 --> 01:55.865
Give it a try.

01:56.908 --> 01:58.118
Does it fit?

01:59.202 --> 02:00.662
[Won-jun] What do you think?

02:00.745 --> 02:02.539
- Ooh!
- [Doona] Ooh! It's nice.

02:02.622 --> 02:03.957
[Won-jun] It really is nice.

02:04.040 --> 02:06.251
- [Doona] Wanna get these?
- Okay, let's get them.

02:06.334 --> 02:10.380
[in Korean] ♪ You say ♪

02:11.965 --> 02:17.303
♪ That I'm always a genuine soul ♪

02:19.848 --> 02:25.520
♪ You also say ♪

02:26.563 --> 02:29.983
♪ That at least for today ♪

02:30.066 --> 02:32.610
♪ I am everyone's lover ♪

02:35.113 --> 02:39.826
♪ Tonight the clowns' farce
Wins applause ♪

02:42.704 --> 02:47.500
♪ As once again
The fake masquerades as art ♪

02:50.378 --> 02:53.089
[in English] ♪ Wear your leather… ♪

02:53.173 --> 02:55.133
MOM

02:55.216 --> 02:56.176
[phone vibrating]

02:58.011 --> 03:03.474
♪ Like a Hollywood movie star… ♪

03:05.643 --> 03:07.353
[crowd cheers]

03:07.437 --> 03:08.646
Whoo!

03:09.147 --> 03:10.064
Whoo!

03:10.648 --> 03:11.733
MOM

03:11.816 --> 03:13.443
- [phone vibrating]
- Oh, um…

03:20.783 --> 03:26.331
[in Korean] ♪ I sometimes ♪

03:27.999 --> 03:34.380
♪ See myself in you ♪

03:36.090 --> 03:42.180
♪ One day ♪

03:42.847 --> 03:43.681
♪ My ugly… ♪

03:43.765 --> 03:44.766
[Won-jun in English] Okay.

03:45.642 --> 03:46.809
Well,

03:46.893 --> 03:50.063
then you should probably do
what the doctor says. Don't you think?

03:50.146 --> 03:52.523
So, hey, listen, Mom.
We need to make a decision really soon.

03:52.607 --> 03:54.609
Once we do,
they can schedule the operation for her.

03:55.526 --> 03:56.361
Okay then.

03:57.654 --> 03:58.863
[phone beeps]

04:00.073 --> 04:00.907
[sighs]

04:02.158 --> 04:04.452
MINSONG NATIONAL UNIVERSITY
DEPARTMENT OF CLOTHING

04:04.535 --> 04:06.079
[overlapping chatter]

04:07.121 --> 04:09.290
COME PICK ME UP RIGHT NOW
I'M TOO DRUNK TO WALK

04:09.374 --> 04:11.834
[chuckles] Okay, I sent it.

04:11.918 --> 04:12.835
[chuckles]

04:12.919 --> 04:14.087
Oh, you know,

04:14.837 --> 04:17.382
it's gonna be embarrassing
if no one comes.

04:17.465 --> 04:18.466
[laughs]

04:18.549 --> 04:20.176
Well, then it's not meant to be.

04:21.302 --> 04:23.096
[I-ra groans]

04:23.179 --> 04:27.225
- [girl] To her destiny! Woo-hoo!
- [girl 2] To destiny! Cheers!

04:41.447 --> 04:45.326
So I went to my fortune teller,
and she said today I'll be lucky in love.

04:45.410 --> 04:46.452
- Seriously? Awesome!
- Yup.

04:46.536 --> 04:48.538
- Can I hang out with you?
- Of course.

04:48.621 --> 04:49.622
Yes!

04:50.915 --> 04:53.126
[I-ra] Can you come right now
to pick me up?

04:53.209 --> 04:55.086
- I'm too drunk to walk.
- [gasps]

04:57.630 --> 05:00.466
Uh, um… hey, I… I gotta bounce, dude.

05:00.550 --> 05:01.384
Huh?

05:01.467 --> 05:02.885
It's just, I gotta go right away.

05:02.969 --> 05:04.178
- Hey, where you going?
- Huh?

05:04.262 --> 05:05.096
- I'm sorry.
- Don't go.

05:05.179 --> 05:07.015
- Let me go.
- I thought we were gonna hang out!

05:07.098 --> 05:08.725
[Yun-taek] Look, look…
Chill. I'll be back.

05:08.808 --> 05:10.268
- Hey!
- [Yun-taek] See you later!

05:10.351 --> 05:13.563
[girl] Useless jerks, all of them. Pssh.

05:15.106 --> 05:16.441
- [bell jingles]
- Ugh!

05:18.818 --> 05:20.778
[gasps] Someone's here.

05:21.529 --> 05:22.655
- Oh!
- [snorts]

05:22.739 --> 05:24.949
Look, someone came.
Look over there. He's standing.

05:25.908 --> 05:27.035
Oh…

05:27.118 --> 05:28.745
What the fuck? She was right.

05:29.871 --> 05:30.997
[scoffs]

05:31.080 --> 05:31.998
Hey.

05:32.081 --> 05:34.417
- Wake up, I-Ra. Hey. Come on. Wake up.
- [I-ra groans]

05:34.500 --> 05:35.960
Wake up. Wake up.

05:39.630 --> 05:40.798
[I-ra] Huh?

05:40.882 --> 05:42.884
[romantic music playing]

05:55.730 --> 05:59.609
- All right, we're home!
- Let go of my ears.

05:59.692 --> 06:02.487
[laughs] We made it!

06:03.780 --> 06:04.614
I'm tired.

06:04.697 --> 06:06.407
[I-ra laughing]

06:06.491 --> 06:09.077
- [I-ra] Hey. No wait! Ah.
- [Jeong-hun grunts]

06:09.160 --> 06:10.661
- [sighs]
- [I-ra groans]

06:11.746 --> 06:12.747
[Jeong-hun sighs]

06:13.414 --> 06:14.832
[I-ra groans]

06:21.381 --> 06:23.341
When you look at me like that,

06:23.424 --> 06:24.926
it makes me wanna make out.

06:39.607 --> 06:41.442
Ugh, hey!

06:41.526 --> 06:44.404
Why'd you move so fast? Did you dodge me
'cause you don't know how to kiss?

06:44.487 --> 06:47.949
- It's 'cause you're drunk.
- Well, thanks to you, not anymore!

06:48.616 --> 06:51.077
- Well, are you sure?
- Yes, totally.

06:52.245 --> 06:53.121
[I-ra] Hmm?

06:53.204 --> 06:54.831
[emotional music playing]

06:58.751 --> 06:59.794
I like you too, I-ra.

07:01.129 --> 07:03.005
See? I'm not the only clueless one here.

07:07.635 --> 07:08.678
Wow.

07:10.805 --> 07:11.931
What now?

07:12.640 --> 07:14.434
He's so freaking hot.

07:21.482 --> 07:22.316
[I-ra sighs]

07:35.413 --> 07:36.747
[emotional music playing]

07:47.049 --> 07:50.887
- [gasps] Do you know how cute you are?
- Yes, you are very cute, aren't you?

07:50.970 --> 07:56.142
- His face is squishy like tofu, isn't it?
- Tofu, tofu, Won-taeky, tofu!

07:56.225 --> 07:57.435
- Stinky tofu!
- I know.

07:57.518 --> 08:00.313
- I love his jacket as well.
- It looks like stinky tofu! [chuckles]

08:00.396 --> 08:03.107
- It's Yun-taek, all right?
- You look like stinky tofu. [laughs]

08:03.191 --> 08:04.567
- Taeky, Won-taeky!
- Won-taeky!

08:04.650 --> 08:05.818
- Let's have another!
- Okay.

08:05.902 --> 08:08.196
Your friend I-ra,
how come she's not here?

08:08.279 --> 08:10.406
- Toast!
- Let's drink to us, okay?

08:10.490 --> 08:12.992
- All right! Cheers!
- Cheers!

08:13.075 --> 08:14.952
- Mmm!
- Mmm!

08:15.036 --> 08:17.205
[gasps] You drink like such a stud!

08:17.288 --> 08:19.832
- Wait, what's this? It's a dimple, right?
- That was really good.

08:19.916 --> 08:21.834
- [gasps] He even has dimples!
- Ah!

08:21.918 --> 08:23.544
- So cute!
- Your dimples are so cute!

08:23.628 --> 08:25.922
- You're dressed so well today.
- I can't even believe it!

08:26.005 --> 08:28.382
- Let's do this thing right.
- Oh!

08:28.466 --> 08:31.135
- The stinky tofu is stripping for us!
- I'll pour this time.

08:31.219 --> 08:33.721
- [girl] Ah!
- That's great. That's great. Yeah!

08:33.804 --> 08:35.765
- Yeah! Let's go!
- Okay!

08:35.848 --> 08:37.016
[girls laugh]

08:42.897 --> 08:43.940
[inhales deeply]

08:44.690 --> 08:45.566
[exhales]

08:58.037 --> 09:03.793
[in Korean] ♪ You say ♪

09:05.253 --> 09:10.716
♪ That I'm always a genuine soul ♪

09:13.302 --> 09:18.224
♪ You also say… ♪

09:18.307 --> 09:20.184
[crowd cheering]

09:20.268 --> 09:23.396
♪ That at least for today ♪

09:23.479 --> 09:25.731
♪ I am everyone's lover ♪

09:28.401 --> 09:32.822
♪ Tonight the clowns' farce
Wins applause ♪

09:36.200 --> 09:37.034
♪ As once again… ♪

09:37.118 --> 09:39.620
- [crowd cheering]
- [pop music playing]

09:52.300 --> 09:56.012
[in English]
♪ Step, step, step, step, step ♪

09:56.512 --> 09:59.640
♪ Step, step, step, step, step ♪

10:00.433 --> 10:01.726
[exhales]

10:06.188 --> 10:08.190
[gentle music playing]

10:17.950 --> 10:20.870
[in English] ♪ I just realized… ♪

10:28.127 --> 10:30.129
[emotional music playing]

11:08.668 --> 11:10.086
[Doona] Whoo!

11:10.920 --> 11:11.837
Whoo!

11:20.054 --> 11:22.181
- Yay!
- [Won-jun] Whoo!

11:22.264 --> 11:24.266
[emotional music continues]

11:31.565 --> 11:33.859
[sighs] It's so nice.

11:34.777 --> 11:35.903
[Won-jun chuckles]

11:35.986 --> 11:38.739
Your taste in things is very predictable.
You know that?

11:40.408 --> 11:41.534
I know it is.

11:42.493 --> 11:44.495
I've always been this way.

11:45.871 --> 11:47.498
I like things that are ordinary.

11:47.998 --> 11:49.750
Well, you're not ordinary.

11:49.834 --> 11:50.710
Hmm.

11:51.794 --> 11:52.712
[Won-jun chuckles]

12:06.434 --> 12:08.394
[Won-jun] Do you ever wish
you could go back?

12:10.438 --> 12:12.189
- Hmm?
- You were a singer, hmm?

12:13.607 --> 12:16.277
I'm sure that you miss it
'cause it was your life at the time.

12:17.069 --> 12:18.404
You were born to perform, I think.

12:23.409 --> 12:24.452
Would you allow it?

12:25.035 --> 12:26.162
[chuckles]

12:26.245 --> 12:29.582
What kind of question is that?
If you want to perform, you should.

12:31.667 --> 12:33.419
I'd love to see you sing, you know?

12:35.880 --> 12:37.631
I would support you no matter what.

12:50.394 --> 12:52.438
I forget sometimes how naive you are.

12:58.444 --> 13:00.362
What if they say we can't be together?

13:01.280 --> 13:02.281
Then what?

13:04.575 --> 13:05.409
Uh…

13:06.494 --> 13:08.496
[somber music playing]

13:13.167 --> 13:14.251
[Won-jun] Hello?

13:14.335 --> 13:15.961
Your voice sounds scratchy.

13:17.254 --> 13:18.631
Are you feeling all right?

13:19.173 --> 13:20.466
[Won-jun] I'm okay.

13:21.091 --> 13:22.051
[Doona sighs]

13:22.676 --> 13:24.595
[Won-jun groans] I just got here,

13:24.678 --> 13:25.888
and I miss you already.

13:28.098 --> 13:29.183
So do I.

13:33.938 --> 13:35.648
Has it been raining there at all?

13:37.775 --> 13:38.692
[Won-jun] No.

13:39.401 --> 13:41.028
It's overcast, but no rain yet.

13:50.496 --> 13:53.082
Apparently, this year,
we're supposed to get a lot of rain.

14:07.221 --> 14:08.597
[line ringing]

14:13.644 --> 14:14.770
[glass cracking]

14:27.908 --> 14:29.368
[somber music playing]

14:47.428 --> 14:49.763
I SAW MY LOVE DOONA
AT THE NERD CONNECTION CONCERT

14:49.847 --> 14:51.223
DOONA THE GODDESS! BEAUTIFUL!

14:51.307 --> 14:54.602
[crowd chanting] Lee Doona!
Lee Doona! Lee Doona!

14:54.685 --> 14:56.645
LEE DOONA MADE A SURPRISE APPEARANCE

14:56.729 --> 14:59.273
[crowd chanting] Lee Doona! Lee Doona!

14:59.356 --> 15:01.358
[clapping]

15:07.865 --> 15:09.867
[somber music continues]

15:25.799 --> 15:27.509
[inhales deeply]

15:33.515 --> 15:35.726
LAWSUIT NOTICE FOR DAMAGE CLAIM
FROM BREACH OF CONTRACT

15:35.809 --> 15:37.061
[man] Hello.

15:37.144 --> 15:40.731
I'm Jung Ji-guk, the legal representative
of MSA Entertainment.

15:41.357 --> 15:44.360
My client has commenced proceedings
against you for financial damages

15:44.443 --> 15:47.071
arising from the breach
of your exclusive contract.

15:47.154 --> 15:49.782
I believe you received
the notice via certified mail.

15:50.282 --> 15:53.410
Moving forward, I'd prefer
to liaise with your legal representative

15:53.494 --> 15:54.453
rather than yourself.

16:02.127 --> 16:03.170
[sighs]

16:04.922 --> 16:05.798
[sighs]

16:09.551 --> 16:10.928
[breathes shakily]

16:11.011 --> 16:13.013
[mysterious music playing]

16:15.474 --> 16:16.392
[sighs]

16:21.480 --> 16:22.481
[exhales shakily]

16:24.900 --> 16:26.860
[sniffles]

16:26.944 --> 16:27.778
[sighs]

16:27.861 --> 16:29.279
[phone vibrating]

16:29.780 --> 16:30.698
[sniffles]

16:38.247 --> 16:41.750
LAWSUIT NOTICE FOR DAMAGE CLAIM
FROM BREACH OF CONTRACT

16:41.834 --> 16:45.212
YOU HAVE INCURRED A PENALTY
DUE TO YOUR UNILATERAL BREACH OF CONTRACT

16:57.891 --> 16:59.226
[Doona] Don't smoke in here.

17:07.901 --> 17:09.611
Did you really
have to take things this far?

17:12.990 --> 17:14.616
You think this is all my doing?

17:18.954 --> 17:19.788
[sighs]

17:21.165 --> 17:22.583
I would've taken things farther.

17:22.666 --> 17:25.169
As I recall, we agreed
to terminate the contract

17:25.252 --> 17:27.713
on the condition
I wouldn't sign elsewhere.

17:32.468 --> 17:34.386
Did you really think that was possible?

17:35.137 --> 17:36.638
I may have washed my hands of you,

17:37.765 --> 17:39.600
but it won't be as easy with President Ma.

17:42.061 --> 17:44.021
You set a bad precedent in this industry.

17:44.104 --> 17:46.565
They're not letting someone like you
off the hook like that.

17:50.235 --> 17:51.737
So what happens next?

17:51.820 --> 17:54.948
Regardless of the compensation,
they'll make this trial drag on endlessly,

17:55.032 --> 17:56.950
because it's their way of torturing you,

17:57.034 --> 17:58.994
all the while,
destroying your public image

17:59.078 --> 18:01.914
with a smear campaign
with no regard for the truth.

18:01.997 --> 18:03.624
How will you make a comeback then?

18:05.042 --> 18:06.543
Your career will be completely over.

18:19.389 --> 18:21.308
So just say what I should do, then.

18:21.892 --> 18:23.102
You should already know.

18:23.852 --> 18:25.395
This'll be your last chance, you got it?

18:26.313 --> 18:28.607
I've taken care of the videos
posted online.

18:28.690 --> 18:31.485
Now, it's time for you
to get rid of that guy.

18:32.069 --> 18:33.112
If you make a comeback,

18:33.195 --> 18:35.447
he'll be the first thing
they'll rip to shreds.

18:38.575 --> 18:40.410
[Won-jun and Kooksu laughing]

18:40.494 --> 18:43.163
- [Kooksu] Hey, you get everything?
- [Won-jun] Of course. I got it all.

18:43.247 --> 18:44.081
Oh, good, I do too.

18:44.164 --> 18:46.291
- We have enough?
- Yeah, dude, for sure.

18:46.375 --> 18:48.293
- Do you have your keys?
- Yeah, left pocket.

18:48.836 --> 18:50.003
[Won-jun] Hmm…

18:50.504 --> 18:51.421
Got it.

18:53.090 --> 18:54.091
[Kooksu shivers]

18:55.384 --> 18:57.594
[Kooksu] Hey, what are you wearing?
Is that a ring?

18:57.678 --> 18:59.096
Did you get a girlfriend?

18:59.179 --> 19:00.430
You finally noticed.

19:00.514 --> 19:01.849
[Kooksu] You should've told me!

19:01.932 --> 19:03.559
- Well, is she hot?
- Very.

19:03.642 --> 19:05.144
What the hell, man?

19:05.227 --> 19:07.187
- I wanna meet her.
- [chuckles] All right, you will.

19:07.271 --> 19:09.982
You gotta tell me
how I can meet a pretty girl too.

19:10.065 --> 19:12.067
[rain pattering]

19:15.237 --> 19:17.156
[Won-jun] Won-yeong
is being discharged on Sunday.

19:17.239 --> 19:20.159
I'll deal with that and come up
right after, even if it's late.

19:20.742 --> 19:22.035
Okay, gotta go, Doona.

19:23.162 --> 19:24.621
Okay, bye.

19:24.705 --> 19:25.706
[Won-jun] I'll call you.

19:35.883 --> 19:36.758
[sighs]

19:42.139 --> 19:44.057
I'm off to Na-yeong's. I'll see you later!

19:44.141 --> 19:45.893
Oh! Here. Take this.

19:47.227 --> 19:48.270
It's from Doona.

19:49.438 --> 19:50.564
Thanks so much, Doona.

19:51.773 --> 19:53.275
- See you.
- [girl] Bye.

19:55.694 --> 19:57.404
[door beeps]

19:57.487 --> 19:58.405
[Jin-ju chuckles]

19:58.488 --> 20:01.366
You didn't need to bring gifts, seriously.
[chuckles]

20:01.450 --> 20:03.202
I heard you're taking time off.

20:03.285 --> 20:04.244
Yeah.

20:04.328 --> 20:07.247
My father used to pay
for my tuition fees, so I'm broke.

20:07.748 --> 20:11.251
Besides, it's hard to see
you and Won-jun together, so I need space.

20:11.793 --> 20:14.004
You don't have to be
quite so honest, you know.

20:14.087 --> 20:15.005
[both chuckle]

20:15.505 --> 20:17.758
Oh, I got a new job,
so next meal's my treat.

20:20.344 --> 20:22.721
So I guess this must mean
that you don't hate me that much?

20:23.805 --> 20:24.973
Hmm…

20:25.807 --> 20:27.351
How could I possibly hate you?

20:27.851 --> 20:30.687
My father has run for office
three separate times and always lost.

20:31.396 --> 20:34.191
And every time he loses,
he'll talk trash about the winner.

20:34.691 --> 20:35.651
Honestly, though,

20:36.276 --> 20:39.196
is it really the winner’s fault
for winning? [chuckles]

20:39.279 --> 20:40.948
Blaming the winner when you lose

20:41.031 --> 20:44.493
is really only going to make you
look a lot more pathetic. It's a bad look.

20:47.621 --> 20:48.997
If I'm being honest,

20:49.539 --> 20:51.124
your dad is totally a jerk.

20:53.710 --> 20:55.045
I talked with him once.

20:56.296 --> 20:58.090
It was the night
you passed out at my house.

20:59.299 --> 21:02.094
- Um, yes, hello?
- [Jin-ju's dad] You crazy bitch.

21:02.177 --> 21:05.222
What kind of lowlifes are you out with
at this time of night?

21:06.890 --> 21:08.600
Ugh! No way!

21:09.726 --> 21:11.144
I had no idea.

21:11.645 --> 21:12.646
[laughs]

21:13.814 --> 21:14.731
Oh.

21:14.815 --> 21:17.859
That's when I started
to really feel for you.

21:18.860 --> 21:22.447
I felt awful you were trying so hard
to appear like nothing was wrong.

21:24.866 --> 21:26.702
Ugh, this is super embarrassing.

21:26.785 --> 21:29.288
Don't feel embarrassed.
Friends don't judge.

21:29.371 --> 21:30.998
I've been living life all wrong.

21:31.665 --> 21:33.875
Ignoring my problems
doesn't solve anything.

21:33.959 --> 21:34.876
Mm-mm.

21:36.128 --> 21:38.714
Plenty of people
are living their lives wrong.

21:38.797 --> 21:39.798
You're not one of them.

21:40.382 --> 21:41.216
[Jin-ju] Hmm.

21:46.638 --> 21:48.056
So what brought you here, Doona?

21:51.351 --> 21:52.311
I just missed you.

21:54.271 --> 21:55.939
You're a friend. I told you that.

22:19.463 --> 22:21.465
[somber music playing]

22:56.208 --> 22:57.084
[sighs]

23:53.974 --> 23:55.976
[mysterious music playing]

24:11.408 --> 24:12.325
[ring clatters]

24:30.343 --> 24:34.598
NOWDROWZ
INSOMNIA, NON-HABIT-FORMING, SLEEP AID

25:18.517 --> 25:19.726
Oh, you're up.

25:20.310 --> 25:21.561
Want some coffee?

25:22.646 --> 25:23.563
Okay.

25:24.105 --> 25:25.440
I'll make the toast, then.

25:45.919 --> 25:46.920
[car beeps]

25:56.263 --> 25:58.056
[engine starts]

25:59.808 --> 26:01.810
[tires squeal]

26:05.021 --> 26:06.189
[footsteps approaching]

26:08.775 --> 26:09.943
[tires screech]

26:29.921 --> 26:32.424
Go ahead. Talk. I assume
there's something you want to say.

26:32.507 --> 26:35.302
I need you to stop…
whatever business you have with her.

26:37.304 --> 26:38.680
And leave her alone for good.

26:39.180 --> 26:40.932
And no more personal visits. You got that?

26:41.683 --> 26:42.517
[In-wook sighs]

26:43.226 --> 26:44.978
Why are you so angry over all this?

26:45.854 --> 26:48.064
You're about 21, 22, right?

26:48.148 --> 26:49.608
Is your military service done yet?

26:50.191 --> 26:52.736
So by the time you finish university
and find a job

26:52.819 --> 26:55.947
and whatever else you might do,
that's at least five years more.

26:57.157 --> 26:59.034
Do you really plan on
dating her till then?

26:59.868 --> 27:01.661
- Realistically speaking--
- I certainly hope so.

27:04.873 --> 27:06.041
Okay, kid.

27:06.541 --> 27:08.001
I bet you're also the type

27:08.084 --> 27:10.837
to believe in things
like fairies and ghosts

27:10.920 --> 27:15.091
or past-life connections, right?
I guess it's easier when you're a kid.

27:15.175 --> 27:17.552
Then why don't you let us kids
figure it out ourselves?

27:17.636 --> 27:19.971
Too much is riding on this
for me to do that. Sorry, kid.

27:20.055 --> 27:22.223
[scoffs] Quit exaggerating.

27:26.227 --> 27:27.187
I wasn't exaggerating.

27:28.396 --> 27:30.690
All that really matters
is what the public thinks of her,

27:30.774 --> 27:33.943
and letting her come back
after how she acted is a big risk for us.

27:34.027 --> 27:36.488
Her current approval rating
has hit rock bottom.

27:36.571 --> 27:38.281
No one knows what to expect at all.

27:38.365 --> 27:40.492
If Doona alone
stood to make ten billion won,

27:40.575 --> 27:43.036
well then, I'm sure
we're risking ten times that.

27:43.119 --> 27:45.080
Given what's already at stake,
no one's dumb enough

27:45.163 --> 27:47.082
to add a boyfriend to the equation.
You got it?

27:47.165 --> 27:49.501
Not the label, not even Doona.

27:52.504 --> 27:54.005
So who should leave who alone?

27:54.798 --> 27:55.632
Take a guess.

27:59.594 --> 28:01.304
[dramatic music playing]

28:24.661 --> 28:25.829
[sighs]

28:29.666 --> 28:31.668
[bus approaching]

29:18.548 --> 29:21.009
[In-wook] I think Doona
has had a lot to think about,

29:21.092 --> 29:22.886
and ultimately,
what she wants from the company

29:22.969 --> 29:26.181
is to give her a little bit more say
in all her future work.

29:26.681 --> 29:28.475
What do you think, President Ma?

29:28.558 --> 29:30.769
Oh, of course. She should have a say

29:30.852 --> 29:32.771
and make the kind of music
she really likes.

29:32.854 --> 29:33.813
So moving forward,

29:33.897 --> 29:35.732
the company will allow Doona
to be creative lead

29:35.815 --> 29:37.650
and take the music
any direction she wants?

29:37.734 --> 29:40.069
[Ma] Yes. Why would we interfere, huh?

29:40.153 --> 29:41.654
She can make whatever.

29:41.738 --> 29:45.283
After all, she's the songwriter here,
and our job is to support her, right?

29:45.366 --> 29:48.453
Doona, moving forward,
please feel free to do what you want.

29:48.536 --> 29:50.371
You can make the music you like, hmm?

29:50.955 --> 29:53.625
How many tracks did you say
were already in the works?

29:54.125 --> 29:56.377
[In-wook] We have about five or six songs
featuring artists

29:56.461 --> 29:58.630
that Doona herself selected. Hmm.

30:01.508 --> 30:04.260
If there's anything you need right away,
ask Mr. Ko.

30:05.178 --> 30:07.597
I'll handle the move,
so you don't need to worry about it.

30:08.556 --> 30:11.100
But let me know if there's
anything you need from the house, okay?

30:13.186 --> 30:14.646
[Doona] It's strange, isn't it?

30:15.772 --> 30:17.190
That I can sing again.

30:17.941 --> 30:19.526
I didn't think I'd be able to.

30:22.237 --> 30:24.072
[sighs] How should I let him go?

30:25.323 --> 30:27.408
You're good at discarding people, right?

30:28.159 --> 30:29.410
So what should I do?

30:30.620 --> 30:31.538
Tell me how.

30:33.748 --> 30:35.875
How should I break Won-jun's heart, huh?

30:36.668 --> 30:38.878
Because I don't have it in me to do it.

30:42.715 --> 30:43.633
I'll sing

30:44.968 --> 30:48.513
and dance well enough to justify
the money that's been re-invested in this.

30:49.764 --> 30:52.267
More than enough
for them to forget their losses.

30:52.350 --> 30:55.353
And, you know, I'm not doing this
because of the lawsuit.

30:55.436 --> 30:58.398
- And it has nothing to do with you either.
- I know.

30:59.482 --> 31:03.152
I realized my happiness
is the most important thing. All right?

31:14.831 --> 31:15.915
I met your friend.

31:17.041 --> 31:19.419
He came to my office. He didn't tell you?

31:20.920 --> 31:23.715
From now on, cut contact
with everyone you know. Is that clear?

31:24.799 --> 31:27.093
Get some rest. Tomorrow's a busy day.

31:27.927 --> 31:29.387
What did you say to Won-jun?

31:35.476 --> 31:39.272
There wasn't really much to say.
Not big on entertaining kids.

31:47.739 --> 31:48.656
[door opens]

31:48.740 --> 31:55.121
♪ Like a Hollywood movie star ♪

31:56.414 --> 31:58.416
[cheering and applause]

32:03.838 --> 32:04.881
Thanks a lot, everybody.

32:04.964 --> 32:09.177
I gotta say, tonight's show has been
particularly nerve-racking for me,

32:09.260 --> 32:11.888
and the reason is that I spotted

32:11.971 --> 32:13.765
a familiar face in the audience

32:14.349 --> 32:15.725
earlier this evening.

32:15.808 --> 32:18.311
I mean, I'm a huge fan of hers.

32:18.394 --> 32:21.689
The one and only
Dream Sweet's Lee Doona is here.

32:21.773 --> 32:23.566
[indistinct murmuring]

32:24.734 --> 32:26.069
[lead singer] I'm right, aren't I?

32:27.862 --> 32:32.492
Could I invite you to…
maybe accompany me on stage tonight?

32:32.575 --> 32:34.577
[cheering]

32:36.621 --> 32:39.415
[crowd chanting] Lee Doona! Lee Doona!

32:39.499 --> 32:43.836
Lee Doona! Lee Doona! Lee Doona!

32:43.920 --> 32:49.717
Lee Doona! Lee Doona!
Lee Doona! Lee Doona!

32:49.801 --> 32:51.135
[cheering]

33:13.241 --> 33:17.328
Uh, if you don't mind, do you think
you'd be willing to sing a song for us?

33:17.412 --> 33:19.497
[cheering and applause]

33:26.212 --> 33:28.214
[cheering and applause]

33:38.516 --> 33:40.518
[gentle music playing]

33:51.529 --> 33:54.490
[in English] ♪ I just realized ♪

33:56.826 --> 33:59.912
[in Korean] ♪ The endless winter ♪

34:03.374 --> 34:07.587
♪ And the maze that is my heart ♪

34:15.470 --> 34:17.472
[crowd murmuring indistinctly]

34:46.125 --> 34:48.836
[in English] ♪ I just realized ♪

34:48.920 --> 34:51.839
[in Korean] ♪ The endless winter ♪

34:52.590 --> 34:56.010
♪ And the maze that is my heart ♪

34:56.094 --> 34:58.221
♪ All that time I spent suffering ♪

34:58.304 --> 35:01.224
♪ Pierced by the thorns… ♪

35:01.307 --> 35:02.767
[music fades to silence]

35:04.769 --> 35:05.937
[inaudible]

35:09.899 --> 35:12.276
[dramatic music playing]

35:17.698 --> 35:19.700
[inaudible]

36:11.502 --> 36:12.420
[exhales]

36:45.578 --> 36:48.247
[cascading classical piano music playing]

36:48.331 --> 36:51.167
[panting]

36:53.669 --> 36:55.338
[music fades]

36:56.839 --> 36:59.300
[panting]

37:14.732 --> 37:16.567
[yells]

37:19.779 --> 37:22.281
[panting]

37:26.702 --> 37:29.038
[in English] ♪ I just realized ♪

37:29.538 --> 37:32.250
[in Korean] ♪ The endless winter ♪

37:33.125 --> 37:36.587
♪ And the maze that is my heart ♪

37:36.671 --> 37:39.173
♪ All that time I spent suffering ♪

37:39.257 --> 37:44.804
♪ Pierced by the thorns ♪

37:45.429 --> 37:47.098
[in English] ♪ With love ♪

37:47.181 --> 37:52.728
[in Korean]
♪ Every day felt as heavy as lead ♪

37:52.812 --> 37:54.981
♪ Days passed by ♪

37:55.064 --> 37:57.858
♪ Where I didn't expect
Anything good to happen ♪

37:57.942 --> 38:04.699
♪ And you, a total stranger, came to me ♪

38:05.408 --> 38:08.786
♪ You were a whole other universe ♪

38:10.496 --> 38:15.167
♪ I was a fool back then ♪

38:15.251 --> 38:17.003
♪ Trapped in fear ♪

38:17.086 --> 38:20.214
♪ I didn't understand
Anything about myself ♪

38:20.298 --> 38:25.303
♪ I now realize that my dream is ♪

38:25.386 --> 38:29.849
♪ To spend an ordinary day
Walking by your side ♪

38:30.641 --> 38:35.354
[in English] ♪ I still remember the day ♪

38:35.438 --> 38:38.149
[in Korean] ♪ How you embraced my heart ♪

38:38.232 --> 38:40.901
♪ And how my heart fluttered ♪

38:40.985 --> 38:45.031
[in English] ♪ I still remember the day ♪

38:45.531 --> 38:50.244
[in Korean]
♪ I want to tell you these words now ♪

38:50.328 --> 38:52.955
♪ Stay with me ♪

38:55.041 --> 38:57.668
[in English] ♪ I just realized ♪

38:57.752 --> 39:00.546
[in Korean]
♪ Taking my shaky first steps ♪

39:01.422 --> 39:04.633
♪ I took another step ♪

39:05.134 --> 39:07.470
♪ Held your hand ♪

39:07.970 --> 39:12.683
♪ And smiled so wide ♪

39:14.060 --> 39:15.186
[in English] ♪ With love ♪

39:15.269 --> 39:20.232
[in Korean] ♪ I dug up my feelings for you
And my confusing thoughts ♪

39:20.316 --> 39:23.486
♪ That had been buried deep within ♪

39:23.569 --> 39:27.031
♪ And entrusted them to you ♪

39:28.741 --> 39:33.496
♪ I was a fool back then ♪

39:33.579 --> 39:35.331
♪ Trapped in fear ♪

39:35.414 --> 39:38.501
♪ I didn't understand
Anything about myself ♪

39:38.584 --> 39:43.589
♪ I now realize that my dream is ♪

39:43.672 --> 39:48.219
♪ To spend an ordinary day
Walking by your side ♪

39:48.928 --> 39:53.599
[in English] ♪ I still remember the day ♪

39:53.682 --> 39:55.559
[in Korean] ♪ How you embraced my heart ♪

39:55.643 --> 39:59.146
♪ And how my heart fluttered ♪

39:59.230 --> 40:03.734
[in English] ♪ I still remember the day ♪

40:03.818 --> 40:08.572
[in Korean]
♪ I want to tell you these words now ♪

40:08.656 --> 40:10.866
♪ Stay with me ♪
